## Workspace Crates

All crates live under `crates/` and are versioned together via the workspace `Cargo.toml`:

| Crate | Purpose | Status |
|-------|---------|--------|
| `geometry` | 2D points, affine matrices, path representation, bounding-box helpers | Most complete |
| `svg_dom` | xmltree-based SVG DOM manipulation | Functional scaffold |
| `app_core` | Load/render/save SVG pipeline | Functional scaffold |
| `layout_engine` | Greedy shelf bin-packing algorithm | Functional scaffold |
| `seamly_svg2ezdxf` | SVG DOM → ezdxf intermediate DXF representation | Feature-rich |
| `ezdxf2dxfastm` | ezdxf intermediate → ASTM-D6673-10 DXF file | Functional |
| `cxxqt_bridge` | CXX-Qt bridge: exposes Rust as Qt QObjects — `staticlib`, **Phase 2a–2f complete** | Active |
| `ui_desktop` | Iced desktop UI — **deprecated, planned removal in Phase 17** | Legacy — do not add features |
| `cli` | Command line interface | Functional scaffold |
| `ffi_bridge` | Single `libseamly_core` cdylib re-exporting all C ABI symbols — **planned (Phase 2g)** | Not yet created |

## Qt Frontend (Active — see TODO.md)

The Qt 6.11.1 + QML frontend lives under `qt_frontend/` (Phase 1 and Phase 2a–2f complete).
It replaces `ui_desktop` and calls Rust core crates via the `cxxqt_bridge` CXX-Qt bridge.

| Tool | Version | Purpose |
|------|---------|---------|
| Qt | 6.11.1 | UI framework (LGPLv3); installed at `C:/Qt/6.11.1/msvc2022_64/` |
| CMake | ≥ 3.28 | Qt build system |
| Ninja | any | Build backend (via cmake preset) |
| Qt Modules | Core, Gui, Quick, QuickControls2, QuickDialogs2, Svg, PrintSupport, WebEngineQuick | Required (all LGPLv3 — no GPL modules) |
| cxx-qt | 0.7.3 | Rust→C++ QObject bridge (no manual extern "C" or cbindgen needed) |
| cxx-qt-lib | 0.7.3 | Qt type bindings for Rust (QString, etc.) |
| cxx-qt-build | 0.7.3 | build.rs helper for CXX-Qt code generation |
| cxx-qt-cmake | main branch | CMake integration (`cxx_qt_import_crate`); fetched via `FetchContent` |

**Important cxxqt_bridge constraints:**
- `crate-type = ["staticlib"]` — linked into SeamlyLayout executable
- `edition = "2021"` — **not** `"2024"`; `cxx-qt-build 0.7.3` incompatible with Rust 2024
- QML registration: use `qmlRegisterType<AppController>(...)` in `main.cpp`; do NOT use `#[qml_element]`
- `#[auto_cxx_name]` on `extern "RustQt"` block: converts snake_case Rust names to camelCase for QML

## C FFI (Phase 2g — Planned)

When Phase 2g begins, `ffi_bridge` will be a single `cdylib` re-exporting all core crate symbols.
Core crates do NOT need `crate-type = ["cdylib"]` individually.
CXX-Qt handles the Rust↔Qt bridge; `ffi_bridge` is only needed for non-CXX-Qt consumers (CLI, etc.).
